## Chronological evidence map (Parakeet recording clock)

| Approximate time | Source-backed action and outcome at cutoff |
| --- | --- |
| ~00:00–00:03 | **Out-of-game** introduction/sponsor and audio recap. Play resumes **at the gelatinous-cube confrontation** from S1E08. **First Sons Brotherhood** (Edgar Boonefellow, Norman Green, Faelan/Faelen Ianya) remains with the three Darkest Delvers. |
| ~00:03–00:12 | First Sons' archer **Norman** fires at cube, **Koh** hits with shortbow and advantage after remaining still. A separate **grick appears behind the party**, blocking the way back; Faelan consults guild guide instead of attacking. **Evelyn's ordinary javelin** hits cube, **Compelled Duel** does not hold it after successful saves. **Piercers fall** from ceiling; Norman struck. **Krandal uses Sacred Flame** on nearby piercer. Cube approaches Evelyn and she dodges its attempted engulfment. |
| ~00:12–00:27 | Koh hits cube again and later damages it with **psychic blade**. The grick drags a piercer and escapes the immediate fight while they struggle with a stalagmite. Faelan casts Thunderwave but is then **engulfed by cube**, temporarily restrained, unable to breathe and harmed by acid (amount unresolved). Evelyn uses **Javelin of Lightning**, command word **“Sparky”** (text only), through a piercer to strike cube; electricity also affects other nearby piercers. **Cube bursts, dies and releases living Faelan**. Krandal had grappled/sat on a piercer in shallow water. First Sons later finish the retreating piercers they can reach; **grick and its captured piercer escape into another tunnel**. Neither the cube nor all underground threats survive/clearance can be conflated. |
| ~00:27–00:39 | Koh **takes a vial of cube gelatin**, uses **one Potion of Healing (6 HP restored)**, and hears scraping deeper in caves. He glimpses a large birdlike creature; guild manual offers an old illustration labeled **“hook horror”** with little explanatory text. The Delvers decide the uncertain beast is not part of their paid contract, and start to retreat. First Sons wants to surface rather than explore further. |
| ~00:39–00:54 | **Hook horror attacks during retreat** rather than being voluntarily hunted. Krandal trips and Evelyn returns to shield/help him; Koh covers retreat with an arrow. One hook strikes Evelyn for **11 piercing HP**, Krandal heals her for **5 HP** while moving. Evelyn blows the **Horn of Blasting a second time**, this time outward into cave, doing **21 thunder damage** and impairing the monster's apparent echo-based navigation; this **does not demonstrate that the horn is destroyed**, and the previously noted crack remains a caution. Koh then rolls **two natural 20s** on his advantaged shortbow strike, pierces beast through mouth/head; **hook horror dies**. The **cube kill is Evelyn's**, the **hook horror kill Koh's**. |
| ~00:54–01:04 | Party moves back to help First Sons, who are **confronting but not fighting** the grick as it withdraws still holding a piercer. Evelyn piles rocks/boulder to **obstruct one side passage**, not a comprehensive concrete seal of all caves. Koh carves **one large hook limb** from dead horror, then sees **a second living hook horror** approach and nuzzle the corpse; stealthily escapes with trophy. Group traverses previously encountered traps and returns safely through opening **into Pelor's temple about 4 PM**. No later fight with surviving horror/grick. |
| ~01:04–01:09 | **Brother Maynard** protests the ruined Hall of Penance mosaic; **Carrie Underworld** surveys old entrance using an instrument. Delvers tell them about cube and hook horror. **Evelyn hands Carrie the Horn of Blasting**, requesting it be used to help future fighters; **Koh submits the hook trophy, his vial of cube gelatin, and one psychic-responsive spear/shaft** for guild examination. Carrie entrusts gathered items to monk courier and orders follow-up at guild. **Submissions, not irrevocable ownership transfers**; return/identification pending. **Do not continue to list the horn as in Evelyn's possession** at cutoff. |
| ~01:09–01:18 | Guild all-bronze follow-up: **Viper Gang** says northeast well yielded nothing; **Brigand Patrol** reports guarding SW square; **First Sons** reports cube, grick-piercer encounter and their own darkmantle/stirges and completed seal; **Five Emissaries** say they cast Fireball into well, no proven investigation of water/monsters. Cassius acknowledges city underground risk, **activates available wood-ranked reserves**, assigns temple-entrance guard and dispatches Carrie to inspect ancient layers. Guild's divinations failed to find tunnels earlier; **possible blocking is speculation**, not demonstrated magic. Cassius says guild will handle temple financial claims, **Delvers won't owe payment to temple**. Citizens should remain calm; bugman rumour from the square still circulating. |
| ~01:18–01:24 | Cassius privately asks Delvers to aid Carrie's temple survey and offers **four possible next-day ruin investigations**: goblins, kobolds, bullywugs or **kuo-toa** fish-people near far eastern wetlands/lake. Delvers **choose kuo-toa mission**, but **no journey or encounter begins this episode**; Aegis's cart planned for next morning. Each Delver **collects 300 gp paid at guild acquisitions desk** for the just-finished well operation; the amount is **per person**, not total or a speculative bounty. |
| ~01:24–01:40 | Back at Pelor's temple, Carrie suspects ancient ruin has **the same layout** as earlier forest site according to field reports, but **physical identity is not established**. Evelyn pushes aside a main sanctuary tapestry, chips stucco to reveal **triangle-and-circle “sky people” carving** under temple wall. **Krandal lifts wooden altar scaffold** off central old stone column, revealing a **five-by-five-inch opening** descending into darkness and issuing a troubling **low drone**, resembling earlier shaft sound. No known bottom reached: Carrie's illuminated pebble drops beyond sight. This is **new sanctuary shaft**, distinct from **previous Hall of Penance pressure-stair opening**. |
| ~01:40–01:48 | An **elf monk collapses** in sanctuary when the droning becomes audible. The party stays conscious. **Causality not proven** by co-occurrence; non-elves do not visibly react. Carrie opts to restore **wooden altar cover**, heavily muffling but not eliminating the sound, instead of descending without guild mission. **Sultan**, who previously gave Koh the climbing sash, appears newly enlisted among **wood-ranked emergency guards** and asks to hold sash; **Koh explicitly does not have it yet**. Sultan's exact guard posting and subsequent action not fully portrayed. |
| ~01:48–02:06 | Party visits southwest well and **Koh actually retrieves his enchanted Sultan's Sash of Climbing**, resolving S1E08 custody. Elder falsely reassured all problems fixed (a **character claim**, not proven potable water or total monster eradication). Koh **replaces his old leather armor with new studded leather** purchased for **45 gp**; offers smith old buckles and previous armor, instead of finishing the old buckle-repair plan. **Krandal commissions a custom face-decorated heavy crossbow for 55 gp**, **pickup promised tomorrow**, not yet carried. From **Goggles Granny**, Krandal **buys one standard healing potion (50 gp)** to replace the one used, and **all three obtain one Potion of Water Breathing each (100 gp each)** for upcoming lake mission; he also receives **three empty vials free**. This is no evidence potions have been drunk yet. |
| ~02:03–02:22 | Evelyn uses Cassius's prior voucher at *Cleaned and Prestidigitation*: armor **cleaned/repaired now** before she delivers it for an enchantment. At **Arcane To Go**, she **purchases an ivory Goat of Travail figurine (300 gp)**, capable according to Gruber's rule explanation of summoning a friendly giant goat for about three hours **once per thirty days**; **the goat is not summoned in the episode**. **Evelyn orders +1 armor enchantment (1,000 gp)**, **delivery due next morning**. Krandal **purchases a Scroll of Detect Thoughts (stated 200 gp at checkout after an inconsistent price conversation)** and **+1 shield (1,000 gp)**; D&D Beyond equipping/selection discussion is table bookkeeping, not proof of early delivery; Gruber says armors and shields ready next morning. **No potion of mind reading or Ring of Mind Shielding bought** (discussed only); no +3 shield despite sheet UI confusion. |
| ~02:22–02:31 | Evelyn briefly visits drinking party at guild then returns to finishing school; Koh visits **daughter Penelope** and his still-bedridden wife. Penelope innocently draws him wielding daggers, while he embellishes cube and mimic as adventure stories **without revealing his actual profession**. Alone with wife he holds her limp, warm hand; medical care remains expensive. He realizes **Psionic Whispers might provide a way to communicate**, but the daily use has already been expended; **he does not contact or cure her this evening**. Krandal meditates/eats a potato in temple dorm and welcomes a small mouse, not an established familiar. |
| ~02:31–02:48 | **Brother Maynard apologizes** for hostility over temple alterations and reveals an unresponsive elf **Rianu Keeves** (phonetic/spelling uncertain), previously meant to officiate Battersby wedding that Krandal performed. He describes failure of ordinary restorative attempts, including **Remove Curse**. Rianu appears asleep/dreaming with a **repeating finger-tap pattern**. Krandal notes possible intentional/military-style code, **writes it down**, does **not decode it**. The **second elf** who collapsed at sanctuary is likewise unresponsive but shows **no tapping/no response to imitated pattern**. Both illnesses' origin and link to drone are **unknown**, and Krandal does **not know about Koh's wife**, so no shared diagnosis. Maynard gives Krandal **Amulet of the Devout (+1)**, traditionally attributed to **Dain Proudface** as maker, and Krandal **accepts and puts it on**; historical attribution is *Maynard's testimony*, not independent verification. |
| ~02:39–02:48 | Evelyn sneaks back into **finishing school** (knocks plant into fountain but reaches dorm), tells roommate **Margaret Dupayton** about adventure. A **bronze ball planning meeting tomorrow at noon** conflicts with kuo-toa journey. Margaret suggests **Alter Self disguise** if she could obtain spell, but **neither acquisition nor impersonation takes place**; Evelyn proposes another sick excuse and friend questions its plausibility. |
| ~02:49–02:53 | **Out-of-game end-of-session GM announcement:** All three have enough XP to reach **level four** and are to take a **long rest before next episode**, choose ability-score improvement/feat later. This is confirmed advance/next-session character state, **not a fully played rest, prepared level-four build or level-five advancement**. Network outro follows. Episode in-world cutoff: party dispersed for the evening, **unresponsive elves remain uncured, altar re-covered, next-day fish mission not yet started**. |

## Continuity, item custody and unresolved questions

- **S1E08 cliffhanger resolved:** Cube **killed by Evelyn's Lightning Javelin**, Faelan rescued alive. A grick **escapes with a piercer**, one additional **hook horror remains alive**, and several passages remain accessible despite previous well-connection sealing. Blocking one side passage with a boulder **does not prove elimination of threats**.
- **Trophies to Carrie/guild:** Evelyn **submits Horn of Blasting** after a second successful blast. Koh **collects then submits** large hook limb, vial of cube gelatin and one psychic spear/shaft; no final testing/return shown. Remaining spare shafts and six inserted in plates cannot be freely assigned to the party without proof.
- **Temple:** Hall of Penance entrance from S1E08 remains under guild guard and financial dispute; newly found **main sanctuary altar shaft and drone** are separate. Elves' illness observed, but mechanistic or cosmological explanation unverified. Ancient builder attribution to **Dain Proudface** comes from priestly claim.
- **Koh:** **Actually recovers Sultan's Sash**, replaces leather with studded armor, consumes **one healing potion** earlier and receives **one Water Breathing potion**. Potential future **Psionic Whispers to unconscious wife** remains a hope, not performed contact.
- **Evelyn:** Goat of Travail **purchased, not summoned**; enchantment on cleaned armor **pending morning**; Water Breathing potion obtained. Horn **with Carrie/monk courier for examination**, not proven destroyed or still on Evelyn at cutoff. School meeting at noon threatens her secret, but no disguise made.
- **Krandal:** Purchases **healing potion replacement**, Water Breathing potion, Detect Thoughts scroll and +1 shield (last item's physical delivery due next morning), custom face heavy crossbow **pending**. Receives/actually **wears Amulet of the Devout +1** from Maynard. Observes/records one possible tap code; **does not decode** or solve coma. **300 gp paid to each Delver**, later purchases separate, exact remaining cash not derived.
- **Episode level:** GM explicitly declares **level four for next time**; no confirmed completed long rest in narrated scenes, no settled feat or ability allocation, no field expedition to kuo-toa yet.

